WEBVTT

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.620
Cherry blossoms are
so beautiful!

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:53.020
- Do you like them?
- Yes.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.990
Did you know that a corpse is
buried under every cherry tree?

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.240
A Corpse?

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:16.810
It's the corpse that makes
the blossoms so beautiful.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:25.350
Cherry blossoms are
normally as white as snow.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:34.000
Do you know
what makes them turn pink?

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:41.700
The cherry tree feeds on the
blood of the corpse under it.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.110
The people buried down there-
are they in pain?

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.450
I'll make a bet with you.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.690
A bet?

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.390
Yes, a bet.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.170
When we meet again...

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.880
I can't hear you!
The wind's too loud!

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.970
Sir, the train's coming.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:24.010
Where are you headed?

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.440
Hang on. I'll help you.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:48.400
Train arriving on track 1.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:52.060
Please stay behind
the white line.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.840
Excuse me!

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.290
Oh, no!

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:30.270
The victim is identified
as lkumi Nishimura.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:32.200
Cause of death is stabbing.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:35.310
The suspect is fleeing
down the subway tracks.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.430
I repeat:
the suspect is fleeing.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.750
Can't you describe him
a little better?

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:52.520
I'm sorry. He was far away,
and I didn't see him well.

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:57.120
You have to remember.
You're our only witness.

00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:58.650
Detective Kono!

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:02.460
We can't search
the subway tracks.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.200
First train is going to
take off soon.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:09.500
What if he gets away from us
in the rush-hour crowd?

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:12.770
I wonder if this is a very
well-planned crime-.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.180
Can't you catch him?

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.750
You're our only witness.

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:26.490
We'll be at the scene
of the crime soon.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:27.720
Alright.

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:34.270
He can't stay down here
in the subway forever.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:38.360
If we lose him down here, we'll
have to catch him on the street.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.270
Good luck, Mirei.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:04.190
Are you all right?

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.390
So who is she?

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.230
Is she some sort of medium?

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.570
That's what I thought at first.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.910
It must have been
a shocking sight.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.540
What?

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:35.880
To see someone killed
right before your eyes.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:37.920
How do you know what I saw?

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:41.020
Try to forget it.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.560
No, DON'T forget it!
You have to do a composite sketch!

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:48.330
You too, Mirei.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:54.230
At first, I thought she was
a trained medium, but...

00:08:54.800 --> 00:09:00.080
It was so strange
seeing birds inside the subway.

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:01.310
Birds?

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:08.050
The birds were yours?

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.920
Yes. I'm a medium.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.920
Do you know
what post-cognition is?

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.790
Post-cognition?

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:24.190
I've heard of it, but I didn't know
it really existed.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.460
What is it?

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:29.970
You've heard of premonitions,
haven't you, Hokuto?

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:33.440
That's when you see
what's about to happen.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:40.040
A vision of the future
is called “precognition.”

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:43.480
Post-cognition is just
the opposite of that.

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:45.960
The opposite?

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:51.620
He was about half a head
taller than the victim.

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:58.170
The victim was
5 feet 3 inches tall...

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:04.110
half a head is 5 inches, and
the victim had 2-inch heels on.

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:09.880
That would make the suspect
5 foot 7 to 5 foot 9.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:20.180
He had long, slim eyes,
and a small nose. Thin lips.

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:25.160
Short, straight hair.
His left ear was pierced.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:37.880
I can see into the past.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:43.070
I saw everything that
happened on the subway.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.880
But if you look into the past...

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:52.220
You're about to say that
the past goes back forever.

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:55.690
Yes, the past is infinite.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.250
Then how do you do it?

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:02.290
I don't see the past
with my eyes.

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:04.770
I see it with my fingers.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.300
Your fingers?

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:11.210
Whenever someone is
attacked or killed...

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:17.110
waves of terror
wash over the entire area.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:22.090
It's like a spray of water-.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:26.980
My fingers feel that spray.

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:31.630
I feel the emotions that
people leave behind.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:35.530
So her hands are like sensors!

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:39.670
We put out our hands together
when we measure people's spirit.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:43.230
It's because her fingers
are so sensitive.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:46.170
That's why she
always wears gloves.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:50.550
If she didn't, she might
touch something by accident.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:54.520
She would constantly call up
images from the past.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:12:02.090
So you witnessed
the entire murder?

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:05.660
Yes. The entire scene
was crystal clear.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:08.730
All of it.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:27.480
I've seen so many things
through my fingertips.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:32.750
I've seen things that normal
people never have to see.

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:37.490
Do you know
what a person looks like...

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:41.230
as he kills someone?

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.460
I know far too well.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:53.380
I've seen it too.
Probably not as often as you have.

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:57.110
But I've seen it too.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:01.280
That's true, Subaru.

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:06.120
You've seen things that
most people wouldn't even believe!

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:12.400
She must realize that.
She knows you understand her.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:17.400
But why does she put
herself through that?

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:24.640
I wish I didn't have to see,
but they're depending on me.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:27.410
The police?

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:31.140
No, the victims.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:41.490
Seeing the past
is a dreadful ability.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:45.590
But the lives of espers
have always been tragic.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:46.930
Why?

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:51.370
People are jealous of anyone
who has special powers-.

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:54.460
No matter what those
powers might be.

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:04.350
You met someone
this last spring.

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:05.470
Yes!

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.590
Treasure that man.

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:10.880
I'll be happy, won't I?

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:13.750
So long as you work hard at it.

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:19.700
My friend said you were really
good at telling fortunes!

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:23.360
I'm glad I came!
Thank you very much!

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:24.770
I wish you happiness.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:30.670
Next, please.

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:37.380
You pretty girl, miss.
I give you discount.

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:38.920
Thank you!

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:42.390
Thanks for waiting, Mirei.

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:43.820
No problem.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:45.690
This is for you, Mother.

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:04.670
How strange- Your palm
is a mirror image of mine-.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:10.680
What makes you bring up
such an old story?

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:17.220
When I met you, I couldn't stand
seeing so much of the future.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.790
I was going to stop
telling fortunes.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:24.230
And then I met a
beautiful little girl...

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:26.960
who was looking
so hard into the past.

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:28.830
Mother?

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:33.270
You're the only one who's
ever called me that, Mirei.

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:37.770
It will be time
for me to go soon.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:15.480
I'm sorry. There's nothing
I can do for you.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:23.280
There's nothing I can do.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:29.250
Can't sleep?

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:45.900
What if the murderer gets away?

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:48.410
He'll continue to kill.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:57.390
And Mirei will have to
witness each of those murders.

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:02.460
There must be
something I can do!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:05.260
Her name is Mirei?

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:10.190
She's been putting herself
through this for a long time.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:15.470
She's so brave to
face her own power like that.

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:18.040
She worries me a bit.

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:22.670
Subaru, you're just
a witness in this case!

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.380
- But...
- Here it comes again!

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:30.110
You always think you have to
solve everybody's problems!

00:17:30.810 --> 00:17:34.660
People can only do
so much in their lifetimes!

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:39.560
They're lucky to even BEGIN
fulfilling their potential.

00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:44.000
But you can't do anything
if you let yourself get sick!

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:48.570
You have to eat right and sleep well
before you can help others!

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:50.330
Hokuto...

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:55.340
So, Seishiro, what brings you out
this late at night?

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:59.480
I had a feeling that
Subaru needed me.

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:02.750
A bond between two people
can be very powerful.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:07.490
How true!
How true, Seishiro!

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:12.560
Before long, you might
even start to like Subaru!

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:14.930
Hokuto!

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:22.470
Hey, wasn't there a building here?
Did they tear it down already?

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:26.870
What's he doing so late at night?

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:33.550
Hello!

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:35.950
What are you doing, sir?

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:40.890
Hello. Oh, this?
I'm collecting building scraps.

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:44.090
Building scraps?
How interesting!

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:45.430
Hokuto!

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:48.060
It's my hobby.

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:51.760
Some people collect insect
specimens or animal fossils.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:56.570
But what remains of a building
once it's been torn down?

00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:01.510
I feel sorry for
these great structures.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:05.950
Buildings hold so many events
and memories inside themselves.

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:09.650
Fascinating!
Tell me more about this.

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:12.720
My place is nearby.
Would you like to come over?

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:18.390
You bet! I just bought
the perfect cake for a party!

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:20.800
Hokuto! Don't impose!

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:22.330
That's all right.

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:27.200
But I warn you,
my place is a bit cluttered.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:33.940
Watch your step.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:38.510
Incredible!

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:43.250
It's just a hobby, so sometimes
I'm a bit messy with the pieces.

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:48.180
There's so many! Do you know
what buildings they came from?

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:51.130
Yes, I can tell.

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:03.240
This was part of a hotel.

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:07.040
There's no label!
How can you tell?

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:10.480
Do you know what this is?

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.980
Concrete with some bone in it?

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:19.480
Exactly.
Do you know what kind?

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.160
A human bone.

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:22.690
What?

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:26.770
He must have been buried inside
in a construction accident.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:33.710
Construction was fast and furious
during the post-war period.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:37.540
I found this
in an old scrapyard.

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:40.280
Perhaps he was murdered.

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:43.250
No, it was an accident.

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:47.280
I can tell by touching it.

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:51.980
He can tell by touching it?
Could he be another-

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:07.030
What if there were two
post-cognitives in the world?

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:12.870
And what would happen
when they met?

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:20.880
If they touched fingers,
what would they see?

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:26.090
What would they see?

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:37.630
We're lucky that
Mirei tipped us off.

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:40.930
Or we'd never have known
that the drowning victim...

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:43.940
was actually the first target
of the subway killer.

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:48.810
We found traces of her hair and
clothing on the subway trestle.

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:51.250
Our psychic seems
to be legitimate.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:52.940
Detective Kono?

00:21:53.070 --> 00:21:55.920
Give her a call.

00:21:57.950 --> 00:21:59.220
Right!

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:10.490
Once the weather clears up,
let's go somewhere, Mother.

00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:14.960
Someplace quiet where
we can relax together.

00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:19.040
We're just like a real mother
and daughter, aren't we?

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:23.040
What's wrong, Mother?
You're acting so strange today.

00:22:24.040 --> 00:22:25.850
You've made me so happy.

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:29.890
I'm glad I had the chance
to meet someone like you.

00:22:30.010 --> 00:22:33.050
But I'm afraid
I have to be leaving you now.

00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:35.060
Why?

00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:42.030
You know better than anyone
how well I can see the future.

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:43.360
Mother!

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:48.530
There is a perfect companion
for everyone in this world.

00:22:48.960 --> 00:22:51.380
- More perfect than you?
- Certainly.

00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:53.900
Who?

00:22:57.200 --> 00:22:58.980
Mother!

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:28.310
They're going to be
demolishing this house soon.

00:23:32.170 --> 00:23:34.050
“Daddy”

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:42.360
It's been twelve years.

00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:48.830
I never thought I'd set foot
in this place again.

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:53.240
You want me to recreate
what happened twelve years ago?

00:23:54.230 --> 00:23:59.180
It has always bothered me.
I just need an answer.

00:24:07.070 --> 00:24:10.520
What happened here
twelve years ago?

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:16.830
What did you see
with those glass eyes?

00:24:58.130 --> 00:24:59.430
Mommy!

00:25:00.390 --> 00:25:04.000
Mommy!

00:25:19.080 --> 00:25:20.790
Detective Kono.

00:25:21.450 --> 00:25:23.620
Sorry we're late.

00:25:28.020 --> 00:25:29.590
Mirei.

00:25:34.090 --> 00:25:36.170
It's good to see you again, Subaru.

00:25:44.640 --> 00:25:50.590
A young boy killed his sister
there 12 years ago.

00:25:51.410 --> 00:25:55.520
I met that same boy years later
in juvenile detention.

00:25:56.180 --> 00:26:00.890
His words have
haunted me ever since.

00:26:02.120 --> 00:26:03.900
A reason?

00:26:08.130 --> 00:26:11.200
I didn't have a reason.

00:26:16.640 --> 00:26:19.550
You have incredible powers, Mirei.

00:26:20.140 --> 00:26:21.280
Oh, not really.

00:26:21.410 --> 00:26:24.050
How do you handle it, Mirei?

00:26:24.680 --> 00:26:29.720
I was sad when I first
found out I was different.

00:26:29.880 --> 00:26:34.730
But then I learned that
I wasn't alone.

00:26:36.660 --> 00:26:38.070
A piece of concrete?

00:26:38.190 --> 00:26:40.470
That's all it looks like, but...

00:26:53.010 --> 00:26:54.540
What are you looking at?

00:26:55.380 --> 00:26:57.480
Why did they have to
tear it down?

00:26:57.610 --> 00:26:59.280
They don't need it anymore.

00:26:59.410 --> 00:27:02.790
But there's someone
buried under here.

00:27:02.880 --> 00:27:05.190
Can you see that
with your fingers?

00:27:06.520 --> 00:27:08.020
Kind of.

00:27:10.260 --> 00:27:12.430
Get back.

00:27:17.760 --> 00:27:19.640
Keep this.

00:27:19.770 --> 00:27:23.740
We'll meet again some day.
I promise.

00:27:24.370 --> 00:27:26.440
You promise?

00:27:26.570 --> 00:27:28.520
Yes, I promise.

00:27:39.290 --> 00:27:41.860
We'll meet again some day.

00:27:47.790 --> 00:27:50.100
Do you want something?

00:27:52.130 --> 00:27:53.940
That's my-

00:27:56.300 --> 00:27:58.370
This is 110.
What's the problem?

00:27:58.770 --> 00:28:03.280
All units! Nakano subway,
train 5 is reporting a murder.

00:28:04.280 --> 00:28:07.190
This is car 2,
we're on our way!

00:28:07.310 --> 00:28:09.060
Damn!

00:28:17.220 --> 00:28:18.700
- Detective.
- Who's the victim?

00:28:18.830 --> 00:28:22.270
A middle-aged woman.
Identity unknown.

00:28:25.030 --> 00:28:27.210
Cause of death was strangulation.

00:28:27.330 --> 00:28:29.540
Anything to identify the victim?

00:28:29.670 --> 00:28:34.090
She had a large shoulder bag.
The contents are a little odd.

00:28:43.080 --> 00:28:44.890
Mother!

00:28:46.320 --> 00:28:48.200
“Police Infirmary”

00:28:54.030 --> 00:28:55.840
Mother!

00:28:58.030 --> 00:28:59.700
Subaru...

00:29:00.400 --> 00:29:02.780
Mirei! Thank goodness.

00:29:05.340 --> 00:29:09.520
Detective Kono,
I want to see my mother.

00:29:27.660 --> 00:29:32.370
Mother, was this why
you had to leave me?

00:29:58.460 --> 00:29:59.840
Mirei?

00:30:00.860 --> 00:30:02.310
Detective Kono!

00:30:02.430 --> 00:30:07.110
HQ is calling a meeting.
They think they're closing in on him.

00:30:07.230 --> 00:30:08.710
But how?

00:30:08.840 --> 00:30:10.840
The meeting is starting at four.

00:30:10.940 --> 00:30:14.150
That's only twenty minutes
from now.

00:30:14.270 --> 00:30:16.410
Subaru, I'm going to call a cab.

00:30:16.540 --> 00:30:19.420
Could you see Mirei
back to her house?

00:30:21.350 --> 00:30:24.300
There is no common link
in three murders.

00:30:24.420 --> 00:30:27.130
They've always been too hasty.

00:30:27.450 --> 00:30:30.330
Are you going to catch the killer?

00:30:30.460 --> 00:30:32.800
Don't worry, we'll get him.

00:30:32.930 --> 00:30:34.930
Driver, take them home.

00:30:50.510 --> 00:30:53.960
Thank you for
bringing me home, Subaru.

00:30:54.950 --> 00:30:58.160
Will you be all right
all alone up there?

00:30:58.490 --> 00:31:03.370
I'm more worried about you.
You haven't been sleeping well.

00:31:03.490 --> 00:31:06.200
Don't worry.
The case will be solved soon.

00:31:07.490 --> 00:31:11.470
Yes. So don't worry about it.
Get some sleep.

00:31:12.500 --> 00:31:13.910
Mire“.!

00:31:25.010 --> 00:31:27.720
Sorry to hear about your mother.

00:31:27.950 --> 00:31:30.900
Shouldn't you be at the meeting?

00:31:31.620 --> 00:31:34.500
The meeting at headquarters?

00:31:34.620 --> 00:31:37.760
What a farce!
Those pencil-pushers are so inept.

00:31:45.530 --> 00:31:51.380
You're finally home! Let me
warm up some dinner for you!

00:31:52.370 --> 00:31:56.250
Thanks, Hokuto,
but I'm not very hungry.

00:31:56.380 --> 00:31:59.320
I'll eat something in the morning.
Good night.

00:32:00.510 --> 00:32:01.550
Subaru!

00:32:14.590 --> 00:32:19.940
Good. After all, you're the
only one who can identify him.

00:32:20.030 --> 00:32:22.810
Isn't entrapment illegal?

00:32:22.970 --> 00:32:26.710
Don't worry. The supreme
court has always allowed it.

00:32:26.840 --> 00:32:30.310
The FBI uses this method
fairly frequently.

00:32:30.740 --> 00:32:33.620
It's perfectly safe.
Leave the details to me.

00:32:33.750 --> 00:32:38.060
Train 3 to Marunouchi,
at 12:30 AM?

00:32:38.420 --> 00:32:39.950
Don't forget:

00:32:40.090 --> 00:32:44.930
Sit in the last car,
right-hand side, facing front.

00:32:45.260 --> 00:32:47.300
That's his reserved seat.

00:32:47.430 --> 00:32:48.460
Reserved seat?

00:32:48.600 --> 00:32:50.670
I'll pick you up at 11 tonight.

00:33:57.330 --> 00:34:01.970
Subaru, are you going to
the subway again tonight?

00:34:02.140 --> 00:34:04.980
It's been four days since
I heard from Mirei.

00:34:05.110 --> 00:34:08.180
Maybe I'll find her
on the subway.

00:34:09.680 --> 00:34:13.720
And maybe I can help.

00:34:33.370 --> 00:34:37.140
Detective Sumida has been
taking Mirei onto the subway.

00:34:37.270 --> 00:34:40.250
What are you talking about?

00:34:40.370 --> 00:34:43.620
They've been riding
the 12:30 AM train.

00:34:43.740 --> 00:34:46.850
If we hurry,
we can catch them.

00:35:14.640 --> 00:35:16.810
Protect me.

00:35:28.590 --> 00:35:30.830
Go ahead. I'm stuck.

00:35:41.600 --> 00:35:43.640
What did you say?

00:35:44.740 --> 00:35:47.380
Do I have to tell you again?

00:35:49.680 --> 00:35:51.850
That's my seat.

00:35:52.680 --> 00:35:56.630
That's it? You killed
three people over that?

00:36:02.790 --> 00:36:04.000
Oh, no!

00:36:37.790 --> 00:36:39.290
What happened?

00:36:39.730 --> 00:36:42.540
He had to try his little trap.

00:36:43.400 --> 00:36:46.470
But what good will it do for
his career now that he's dead?

00:36:48.870 --> 00:36:49.940
Mirei...

00:37:09.320 --> 00:37:12.460
I won't let him
get away with this!

00:37:13.360 --> 00:37:16.700
Subaru, I'll call
your sister for you!

00:37:16.830 --> 00:37:20.470
Thank you.
Tell her not to worry.

00:37:35.850 --> 00:37:38.020
I can't feel him.

00:37:42.660 --> 00:37:44.460
Here I am.

00:37:48.860 --> 00:37:52.170
Now it's your turn
to run away.

00:37:52.270 --> 00:37:56.040
If you can run fast enough,
I'll let you go.

00:37:59.040 --> 00:38:01.880
Run as fast as you can.

00:38:02.310 --> 00:38:08.120
It's my turn to be “it,” so I'll
give you until the count of 10.

00:38:08.920 --> 00:38:10.520
One...

00:38:10.650 --> 00:38:11.990
two...

00:38:12.350 --> 00:38:14.130
three...

00:38:14.250 --> 00:38:15.460
four...

00:38:18.960 --> 00:38:20.770
nine...

00:38:21.960 --> 00:38:23.800
ten!

00:38:29.940 --> 00:38:33.780
They said that Subaru's train
has stopped in the tunnel.

00:38:34.210 --> 00:38:38.310
If anyone hurts Subaru,
I'll kill them!

00:38:40.310 --> 00:38:42.490
He'll be fine.

00:38:43.150 --> 00:38:47.960
They said the tunnel comes out
nearby at a maintenance station.

00:38:48.090 --> 00:38:51.500
Let's find the spot
and surprise Subaru.

00:38:52.360 --> 00:38:53.460
Seishiro...

00:39:22.490 --> 00:39:24.430
Stop right there!

00:39:25.860 --> 00:39:28.930
You know,
there are only three bullets left.

00:39:29.130 --> 00:39:32.010
The police only load
four bullets for safety.

00:39:32.130 --> 00:39:35.410
And the detective
already fired once.

00:39:35.970 --> 00:39:37.680
That leaves three.

00:39:37.800 --> 00:39:40.550
You'll have to hit me
in the head or the heart.

00:39:40.940 --> 00:39:44.750
Otherwise, I'll kill you.

00:40:10.600 --> 00:40:11.910
That was a gunshot!

00:40:12.040 --> 00:40:13.710
Mire“.!

00:40:14.040 --> 00:40:15.250
Subaru!

00:40:22.220 --> 00:40:24.390
Gunshots? Seishiro!

00:40:25.520 --> 00:40:28.330
Wait here, Hokuto.

00:40:29.920 --> 00:40:31.060
Take the umbrella.

00:40:31.190 --> 00:40:34.830
I'll be fine.
It's about to stop raining.

00:40:40.730 --> 00:40:42.910
Nice try.

00:40:44.040 --> 00:40:46.480
You nearly got my heart.

00:40:48.140 --> 00:40:50.310
Good bye.

00:40:54.310 --> 00:40:56.620
Climb the ladder.
Get out of here!

00:40:59.090 --> 00:41:00.890
Hurry!

00:42:09.120 --> 00:42:10.360
Miyatake!

00:42:10.460 --> 00:42:13.840
Subaru, help her!

00:42:17.330 --> 00:42:19.070
Mire“.!

00:42:21.230 --> 00:42:22.910
Subaru!

00:42:23.600 --> 00:42:25.610
Hold on tight!

00:42:53.430 --> 00:42:55.610
Come back this way!

00:42:58.240 --> 00:42:59.940
Be careful!

00:43:03.210 --> 00:43:05.710
Nice and slow. Don't slip.

00:43:21.190 --> 00:43:23.370
Mirei, hang on!

00:43:27.200 --> 00:43:28.980
Subaru...

00:43:58.800 --> 00:44:00.940
I promised you.

00:44:02.640 --> 00:44:08.050
I always knew we'd meet again.

00:45:55.310 --> 00:45:57.060
Now you die.

00:46:15.970 --> 00:46:18.410
You may not have Subaru.

00:46:19.170 --> 00:46:22.380
I caught him first.

00:46:27.580 --> 00:46:30.320
I can't hear you!
The wind's too loud!

00:46:46.370 --> 00:46:48.540
Seishiro.

00:47:14.790 --> 00:47:19.070
He didn't really
need a reason to kill.

00:47:20.100 --> 00:47:26.450
But his excuse was that people
were infringing on his territory.

00:47:26.970 --> 00:47:30.220
Subaru!

00:47:33.080 --> 00:47:34.220
Hokuto.

00:47:34.780 --> 00:47:36.820
I was so worried
about you, Subaru!

00:47:37.450 --> 00:47:38.490
Where's Mirei?

00:47:38.620 --> 00:47:40.390
She's fine now.

00:47:40.720 --> 00:47:43.390
The two of them
have already gone.

00:47:43.590 --> 00:47:49.100
It's strange. It almost seems
that they were fated to meet.

00:47:49.500 --> 00:47:54.270
Just like you and Subaru!
Destiny brought you together!

00:47:54.400 --> 00:47:55.500
Oh, really?

00:47:55.940 --> 00:47:58.580
Come on home.

00:47:58.670 --> 00:48:03.420
We'll treat Subaru to
a magnificent breakfast.

00:48:04.840 --> 00:48:07.880
I love a japanese breakfast!

00:48:08.010 --> 00:48:12.480
We can have miso soup with
tofu, natto, and seaweed!

00:48:20.530 --> 00:48:22.400
Come on, Subaru!

00:48:22.530 --> 00:48:24.270
Hurry UP-

00:48:24.960 --> 00:48:26.740
Okay.

00:49:17.950 --> 00:49:23.920
Until our eyes met and I
looked deep down into your soul

00:49:24.560 --> 00:49:29.770
I would not believe
miracles could happen

00:49:30.460 --> 00:49:33.570
Deja vu, I remember

00:49:34.470 --> 00:49:37.970
How we first met
in dreams yet to come

00:49:38.070 --> 00:49:42.080
Memories make me run faster

00:49:44.010 --> 00:49:47.290
Ah, an, an eternity

00:49:47.410 --> 00:49:50.590
I don't want to live forever

00:49:51.120 --> 00:49:55.760
Into your eyes I want just to gaze
and let time freeze

00:49:57.120 --> 00:50:00.590
Never has fate been
something I believe in

00:50:00.890 --> 00:50:05.100
I just want to believe in you

00:50:17.640 --> 00:50:23.620
Spellbound, my heart, held
captive by your mystical charm

00:50:24.120 --> 00:50:26.560
Somehow I know that
I've seen your face before
